WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:07.269
ALAQUA COX [in sign language]
Hey everyone! I'm Alaqua Cox,

00:00:07.321 --> 00:00:11.741
and I play Maya Lopez in
the new series Hawkeye on Disney+!

00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:19.027
TRINH TRAN
We went worldwide to look for

00:00:19.078 --> 00:00:23.611
our Maya Lopez, and we really wanted to
stay true to the characters in the comics.

00:00:23.661 --> 00:00:26.123
ALAQUA COX [in sign language]
I never dreamt of being an actor.

00:00:26.209 --> 00:00:27.745
IVAN
Maybe I rip out your throat.

00:00:27.795 --> 00:00:29.610
Or, maybe, she will.

00:00:30.177 --> 00:00:33.088
ALAQUA COX [in sign language]
A tweet said "female, Native, athletic, smart"...

00:00:33.139 --> 00:00:35.041
Everyone texted me, "This is you!"

00:00:39.687 --> 00:00:41.138
The rest of it's history.

00:00:42.585 --> 00:00:44.409
BERTIE
She's brand new to this whole thing.

00:00:44.459 --> 00:00:48.948
Something that happens with some actors,
that when they step in front of the camera

00:00:48.998 --> 00:00:51.987
there's this kind of, like, collective
inhale of breath, and everyone's like...

00:00:52.037 --> 00:00:52.887
[Gasping]

00:00:52.937 --> 00:00:54.937
She's just got
this star quality to her.

00:00:57.714 --> 00:00:59.188
JEREMY RENNER
Alaqua is amazing.

00:00:59.238 --> 00:01:03.242
She's really just wide-open emotionally,
and was able to contribute a lot.

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:04.105
She's a natural.

00:01:04.155 --> 00:01:05.281
ALAQUA COX [in sign language]
Honestly, I was very nervous.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.498
I didn't know what to do,
because this whole world of acting...

00:01:07.548 --> 00:01:09.592
Everything was new to me.

00:01:09.858 --> 00:01:12.003
BERT
She's an amazing character to have set up,

00:01:12.053 --> 00:01:16.240
and with a new actress like
Alaqua is, that's been such a gift for us.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:22.258
ALAQUA COX [in sign language]
I feel very proud, and I'm excited to show

00:01:22.308 --> 00:01:24.632
everyone that for people
with disabilities, anything is possible.

